# Resenha
The running of many Lince in one computer. In the Resenha mode of Lince, as a TUI, you are able to do this stuff or having one active Lince with a Resenha sand and a backend corresponding set of features to keep using Lince and emulating many more:
- [ ] See all your Lince instances.
- [ ] Add Lince instances.
- [ ] Remove Lince instances.
- [ ] Update each instance separatelly or all at the same time, configuring:
	- [ ] Port of the application.
	- [ ] Directory it is running in.
	- [ ] Name of it's own Local Organ for recognizing in the network discovery.
	- [ ] Known Organs (contacts)
	- [ ] Sync settings between Organs
- [ ] Deterministic Simulation Testing: the runtime that with initial seeded data in possibly any table, random or specific, simulates time, disk and network. If the app is deterministic (and it should be) we should be able to put the same seed and run the Resenha of a Lince or several Lince instances through many years of automated interactions and whatnot, with availability of disk and network differing for writing and access tests, and have the same intended result, the same state in the end. The DNA (Seed) and Runs, the same start produces the same result given the same simulated events of time, network and disk (might be perfection and never reached, but getting as close to it as possible is good). A Run is when we make a seed, ingest in db and do the simulation, of requests coming into Commands, karmas updating naturally, transfers happening, organs syncing, communicating:
	- [ ] Test if Octopii would not solve a lot of our problems in building the parts that simulate time, network and disk for DST: https://github.com/octopii-rs/octopii
	- [ ] Be able to set Constraints, that are enforced, so the state doesnt reach an undesired point. Maybe this means putting a lot of constraints that need to be checked to make sure they are true in one run and not activating them in another, only a part of it. The one with less Constraints will be able to simulate more events per second happening since it doesnt need to be constantly checked to make sure it didnt pass thorugh an undesired state. Similar to the difference of unit tests and end-to-end ones. But instead of it being a division by part it is a division by period of Constraint checking, we can still have a difference of the equivalent of unit tests and e2e and several other types of tests, and still make them be checked in different times.
	- [ ] A seed is a set of .lingua files, that when ingested into Lince makes it behave in a certain way. Having for each part of Lince a Lingua syntax to build it in the db.
	- [ ] Specific tests can be made by running a specific seed on demand.
